==Strategy==
Having most if not all your lineup be surge immune is required, as Malevolent Macho Legs has 100% uptime on its surge with many surges stacking at once and can deal massive DPS. Use meatshields like talented [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cactus Cat]], and [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] (Although not being surge immune, has very high health against Aku/Relics). Your attackers should consist of [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]], or any effective surge immune Uber Rares. [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] is a must-have, being one of the few spammable surge immune attackers, which is very effective against the [[Sir Rel]]s pushing power and for good damage in general. Bringing a Rich Cat is also highly recommended, as money is extremely tight in this stage.

It is also worth noting that [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] will demolish this stage by completely crippling the pushing power of all enemies present and letting you stage all the Surge Immune attackers you want without fear of [[Malevolent Macho Leg Cat]] pushing.

